    "Hoenn & Seek 2.0 (part 4b): a follower Pokémon standing next to each gym leader, Elite Four member and Red.",
    "Read by tools/hoenn/gen_hoenn_followers.py, which appends the objects to each map.json (re-runs replace them).",
    "trainer: the trainer object's graphics_id (unique on its map). species: the ace, i.e. the highest-level",
    "Pokémon of the first team (ties: the trainer's signature Pokémon). at: optional [x, y] to override the",
    "generator's tile choice. local_id: optional name for scripts that need to remove the follower.",
    "The follower uses the trainer's flag, so it hides whenever the trainer does. It doesn't hide on defeat:",
    "every leader here can be battled again.",
    "Not here, for lack of room: Chuck (between the two rocks he smashes), Blaine (in a rock niche) and",
    "Tate & Liza (on a dais whose only open tiles are where you stand to talk to them). Also not here:",
    "Janine (Fuchsia's trick is that every trainer looks like her, and a Venomoth would give the real",
    "one away), Lance and Wallace (their champion rooms run walk-in scenes), Kanto's Elite Four rematch (same",
    "rooms and people as Johto's)."
